        {
          "title": "Datetime Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Types, One Index",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Is",
                "dtype"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Timestamp`",
                  "one point in time",
                  "`datetime64[unit]`"
                ],
                [
                  "`DatetimeIndex`",
                  "index of Timestamps",
                  "`datetime64[unit]`"
                ],
                [
                  "`Timedelta`",
                  "difference of two",
                  "`timedelta64[unit]`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unit: {orange:ns} in pandas 2, {green:us} inferred in pandas 3",
                "Time series work = a ==DatetimeIndex==, **sorted** and unique-ish",
                "It unlocks slicing, `resample` and `rolling('7D')`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Strings and NaT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dates arrive as strings: `str` dtype in pandas 3, `object` before",
                "==Parse first==: nothing time-aware works on string columns",
                "==NaT== is the NaN of dates",
                "NaT **propagates** through arithmetic; most aggregations skip it"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df['date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['date'])"
              ],
              "note": "parse before anything else"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mixing Naive and Aware",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operation on naive vs aware",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "naive `==` aware",
                  "{green:False}, no error"
                ],
                [
                  "naive `<` `>` aware",
                  "{red:TypeError}"
                ],
                [
                  "naive `-` aware",
                  "{red:TypeError}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Check first",
              "text": "Naive has no tz; aware carries one. Run `df.dtypes` and `df.index.tz` before any time work."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Parsing Dates and Building a DatetimeIndex",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Parsing Dates and Building a DatetimeIndex",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Parsing Basics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pd.to_datetime(s)` parses strings, ints, lists → ==datetime64==",
                "Series in → Series; list in → ==DatetimeIndex==",
                "Unparsed date strings stay `str` dtype"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`%Y %m %d`",
                  "year, month, day"
                ],
                [
                  "`%H %M %S`",
                  "hour, minute, second"
                ],
                [
                  "`%b` `%A`",
                  "month name, weekday"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Arguments That Matter",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Argument",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`format='%Y-%m-%d'`",
                  "faster; no day/month guessing"
                ],
                [
                  "`dayfirst=True`",
                  "03/04/2024 = 3 April; default March 4"
                ],
                [
                  "`errors='coerce'`",
                  "bad value → NaT; default `raise` stops"
                ],
                [
                  "`unit='s'` / `'ms'`",
                  "epoch integers → datetimes"
                ],
                [
                  "`utc=True`",
                  "mixed offsets → one UTC column"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Building the Index",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`parse_dates` + `index_col` builds it in ==one step==",
                "Or parse first, then `set_index('date')`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df = pd.read_csv('s.csv', parse_dates=['date'], index_col='date')",
                "# or, step by step",
                "df['date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['date'])",
                "df = df.set_index('date')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Coerce hides bad data",
              "text": "Count the NaT rows: `df['date'].isna().sum()`"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
